Approach: Linear Traversal

Initialize the variable x = 0.

Iterate through every operation in the array.

If the operation contains "+", increment x by 1.

Otherwise, decrement x by 1.

Return the final value of x.

Both prefix and postfix operations have the same effect on the final value, so there is no need to distinguish between them.

























class Solution {
    public int finalValueAfterOperations(String[] operations) {
        int x = 0;

        for (String operation : operations) {
            if (operation.contains("+")) {
                x++;
            } else {
                x--;
            }
        }

        return x;
    }
}
